WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.130
Hold a magnet near a steel paperclip,

2
00:00:02.180 --> 00:00:04.850
and it jumps across and sticks.

3
00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:07.530
Turn the magnet round
and try the other end.

4
00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:10.050
It still pulls the paperclip in.

5
00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:12.570
Now try the same with a second magnet.

6
00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:14.690
One way round they pull together.

7
00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:17.210
Turn one over, and they push apart.

8
00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:20.310
The paperclip only
ever gets pulled in.

9
00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:23.170
Why can't a magnet push
the paperclip away?

10
00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:26.330
In this mission, you'll see
which poles attract and which

11
00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:29.920
repel, and draw the magnetic
field around a bar magnet.

12
00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:33.490
You'll compare permanent magnets
with magnetic materials that

13
00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:35.770
are not magnets themselves.

14
00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:40.580
Your mission: explain why the
paperclip is only ever pulled in.
